      "text": "The second `num_parameters_settable()` returns 2 because `rot` is a `TwoLocal`, which is a blueprint circuit that builds its contents lazily. The `inplace` compose appends `var`'s gates to the unbuilt data, and the later access to `parameters` triggers `_build()`, which rebuilds `rot` from its own configuration and discards the composed gates. Building `rot` before composing keeps the appended gates. I used the private `_build()` method because no public call I could confirm forces the build without changing the circuit's structure.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit.circuit.library import TwoLocal\nimport numpy as np\n\nnum_qubits = 2\n\nrot = TwoLocal(\n    int(np.sum(num_qubits)),\n    \"ry\",\n    [],\n    reps=1,\n    skip_final_rotation_layer=True,\n    parameter_prefix=\"p\",\n)\nvar = TwoLocal(\n    int(np.sum(num_qubits)),\n    \"ry\",\n    \"cx\",\n    entanglement=\"linear\",\n    reps=1,\n    skip_final_rotation_layer=True,\n)\n\nprint(rot.num_parameters_settable())\n\n# FIX: blueprint circuit rot was lazily built, so the inplace compose was discarded when parameters were later accessed -> build rot before composing, because a built circuit keeps the appended gates\nrot._build()\nrot.compose(var, inplace=True)\n\nprint(rot.num_parameters_settable())\n```",
